        { ime: "St Fagans", opis: "In this free open-air museum, opened in 1948, more than forty buildings from all over Wales have been rebuilt stone by stone. A row of miners' cottages is arranged so that each one shows a different period, from 1805 to 1985, so six doors take you through two centuries of everyday life." },
        { ime: "National Museum Cardiff", opis: "The free museum holds one of the best collections of Impressionists outside Paris, assembled by the sisters Gwendoline and Margaret Davies, granddaughters of a mining magnate. Among the paintings are Renoir's “La Parisienne” in her blue dress and Monet's water lilies." },
        { ime: "Cardiff Bay", opis: "On the facade of the Wales Millennium Centre from 2004 are giant letters, which are actually windows, spelling out lines of verse in Welsh and English. The white wooden Norwegian Church by the water was built for sailors, and the writer Roald Dahl, born in Cardiff to a Norwegian family, was baptized there." },
        { ime: "The Victorian arcades", opis: "The city center is crisscrossed by covered shopping passages with glass roofs, the oldest of which is the Royal Arcade from 1858. They house small family shops, cafes and one of the oldest record shops in the world, Spillers Records, founded in 1894." },
        { ime: "Castell Coch", opis: "On a wooded hill north of the city, the same Burges and the Marquess of Bute built a fairy-tale castle with pointed roofs on the ruins of a medieval fortress. The interior is painted with scenes from Aesop's fables, with monkeys, birds and butterflies across the walls and ceiling." }
