        "Belfast grew in the 19th century on linen and shipbuilding, and the Titanic was launched at the Harland and Wolff shipyard in 1911. The partition of Ireland in 1921 left six northern counties in the United Kingdom, and at the end of the 1960s the tension between mostly Protestant unionists and mostly Catholic nationalists grew into a thirty-year conflict known as the Troubles.",
